{
  "version": 1,
  "summary": "verilex proves its own claims in CI: a pinned known-good verilex runs four canary words against the checkout, live, and fails on red, inconclusive or drift.",
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "scripts/ci",
      "summary": "Owns the canary step that CI and developers run.",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "newRange": [
            38,
            43
          ],
          "summary": "The canary step refuses a canary_driver that is not an ancestor of refs/remotes/origin/main.",
          "rationale": "fetch-depth 0 brings every PR commit and every tag into the clone, so a pin to a commit only this branch holds, or a tag named origin/main, could weaken the driver and grade a regression green. The full ref name is used because a tag named origin/main wins over the short name. Verified by scripts/canary-guards tag-origin-main: exit 0 before the fix (commit d979b48), `not on origin/main` after.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-canary-next"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            44,
            61
          ],
          "summary": "The step builds the pinned driver, keeps state and Python bytecode in a mktemp dir, counts word.md directories, and diffs against the merge base.",
          "rationale": "A ledger kept between runs can be forged, so the run is live with --fresh. PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX keeps a planted .pyc from standing in for a word's source. Without a merge base the run is still a live run of every word, so the verdict is the same and only the --changed warnings are lost; the step says so.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-canary-next"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            62,
            75
          ],
          "summary": "The step requires `check: no drift (N admitted)` for N words, and an admitted word in `verilex index` for every claim file, matched literally.",
          "rationale": "check exits 0 on drift and counts only admitted words, so a provisional word or a deleted word with a kept claim would read as no drift. A failing listing sets ok=false instead of exiting, so the summary and kept-evidence line still print. Verified: D1, D2, D3 and the deleted-word attack each exit 1 with the cause named.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-canary-next"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            83,
            85
          ],
          "summary": "scripts/ci runs scripts/canary-guards as its canary-guards step, after canary.",
          "rationale": "The guards are regression tests for the canary step itself, so they run in the same test job and inside the required ci gate.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-canary-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
      "summary": "Runs the canary inside the test job, so the required ci gate covers it.",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "newRange": [
            46,
            47
          ],
          "summary": "checkout fetches full history so git archive finds the pinned driver commit and origin/main exists for the diff.",
          "rationale": "The repository is private, so go install of a SHA needs auth; git archive of a fetched commit does not. Not yet observed on a GitHub runner until this PR's CI runs.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-canary-next"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
